WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.563
Unit 1 is the compliant network check.

2
00:00:02.563 --> 00:00:07.333
It passes only for users connected through
this tenant's Global Secure Access,

3
00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:09.462
from the client or a remote network.

4
00:00:09.462 --> 00:00:13.226
At authentication, it denies
a replayed refresh token.

5
00:00:13.226 --> 00:00:17.328
And with services that support
Continuous Access Evaluation,

6
00:00:17.328 --> 00:00:22.300
such as Microsoft Graph, it rejects a
replayed access token in near real time.

7
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.763
Turning signaling on creates a named
location, All Compliant Network locations.

8
00:00:27.763 --> 00:00:30.470
The pilot policy blocks all resources,

9
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:34.362
for the pilot group, from
every location except that one.

10
00:00:34.362 --> 00:00:39.486
It excludes the emergency access group,
and, following Learn, Microsoft Intune

11
00:00:39.486 --> 00:00:41.693
Enrollment and Microsoft Intune,

12
00:00:41.693 --> 00:00:45.162
to avoid a circular dependency
where devices enroll.

13
00:00:45.162 --> 00:00:48.088
Learn's example sets the
policy straight to on.

14
00:00:48.088 --> 00:00:53.950
The guide, like every library policy, starts
in report-only, for ten business days.
